  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1216 PM CDT Tue Aug 18 2026\n\nOn Thursday, an approaching cold front will maintain rain/storm \nchances throughout the morning hours. Guidance suggests the \npotential that a few storms could become strong to severe with the \nprimary concern being strong/gusty winds and heavy rainfall. The \noverall severe weather chances are low, but non-zero. The front will \nshift to the east by mid-afternoon, which will allow drier air into \nMiddle TN Thursday evening. Troughing and northwest flow will \nsupport additional shower chances Friday afternoon. Fortunately, the \ncoverage should remain rather isolated to scattered at best. This \nweekend looks primarily dry, but isolated showers cannot be ruled \nout. Temperatures appear to stay much more seasonable through the \nweekend and into early next week. Guidance supports high pressure \nsettling in that should limit any widespread precipitation. A \nwelcomed change compared to the recent warmth.",
